Usage: mknod [OPTION]... NAME TYPE [MAJOR MINOR]

Create the special file NAME of the given TYPE.

Type 'p' creates a FIFO: on Windows this is an on-disk marker file
that WinuxCmd commands bridge to a named pipe. Block and character
device nodes have no Windows equivalent and report an error.

OPTIONS:
  -m, --mode ARG       set file permission bits
  -Z                   set the SELinux security context to default type
      --context[=ARG]  set the SELinux security context
      --help           display this help and exit
  -V, --version        output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
